#
# Conformance case: holonic/holonic-band
# AC: ME9 (#775) — holonic levels are PATH-RELATIVE on a genuine multi-parent DAG,
#     and the per-entity min/max depth band is materialized.
#
# This is the positive counterpart to holonic/holonic-level (which proves the
# incoherence violation for a profiled holon occupying NO position). Here a holon
# occupies SEVERAL positions along several paths, so its logic:holonicLevel is
# genuinely path-relative and a non-trivial min/max band exists.
#
# The DAG (a diamond — ex:Sensor has TWO parents):
#
#     Aircraft
#        |  (properPartOf)
#       Wing  ◄─────────────┐
#        |                  |
#     Avionics              |  (Sensor is ALSO a direct proper part of Wing)
#        |                  |
#      Sensor  ─────────────┘
#       / \
#   ChipA  ChipB
#
# So ex:Sensor sits at TWO depths relative to ex:Wing, and both are correct:
#   * direct path  Sensor ⊏ Wing                      → depth 1
#   * via path     Sensor ⊏ Avionics ⊏ Wing           → depth 2
#
# Each reading is reified as its own logic:HolonicPosition (the canonical five-place
# construct: entity, holarchy, context, interval, path) and the two positions differ by
# their logic:positionPath (ex:pathDirect vs ex:pathVia):
#   * ex:posSensorDirect  positionPath ex:pathDirect   (the direct path,  depth 1)
#   * ex:posSensorVia     positionPath ex:pathVia      (the via-Avionics path, depth 2)
#
# Expected derivations for ex:Sensor (ALL all-IRI):
#   * logic:isHolon              — a proper part of Wing/Avionics AND a whole over ChipA/ChipB.
#   * logic:hasHolonicPosition   — occupies positions → NOT charged with
#                                  logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence even though profiled.
#   * logic:multiplyPositioned   — occupies TWO distinct positions (the DAG signature),
#                                  the engine-derived ground that a non-trivial band exists.
#   * NO logic:WeakSupplementation — ChipA and ChipB are disjoint co-parts.
#
# ARCHITECTURE — why no literals here (#775): the foundation chase is ALL-IRI; the native
# foundation evaluator hard-rejects any non-IRI (literal) object. The logic:holonicLevel
# values (1, 2) and the per-entity min/max band are therefore NOT part of this foundation
# world — they are a literal/projection concern that lives OUTSIDE the chase. This case
# proves the engine-verified core of ME9 #2 (path-relativity grounded by
# logic:multiplyPositioned over two distinct logic:positionPaths); the materialized band
# itself is dogfooded as validated ABox data in
# slices/core/logic/examples/holonic-band.ttl. The band endpoints are operator-asserted,
# never engine-derived (the all-IRI chase cannot compare/aggregate integers).
#
# Only ex:Sensor is declared under the logic:MereologyProfile, so the level/coherence
# calculus runs there and there only; ex:Wing and ex:Avionics are holons too but are
# unprofiled, so they are never charged (profile-relativity). ex:Sensor is given TWO
# disjoint proper parts so weak supplementation is satisfied and the case isolates the
# path-relative level band.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so every edge below is
# duplicated there in the named world ex:schema; these are the program axioms.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/holonic/holonic-band/> .

ex:MP a logic:MereologyProfile .
ex:H  a logic:Holarchy .

# The diamond DAG: ex:Sensor has two parents (ex:Wing directly, and ex:Avionics).
ex:ChipA    logic:properPartOf          ex:Sensor .
ex:ChipB    logic:properPartOf          ex:Sensor .
ex:Sensor   logic:properPartOf          ex:Wing .
ex:Sensor   logic:properPartOf          ex:Avionics .
ex:Avionics logic:properPartOf          ex:Wing .
ex:Wing     logic:properPartOf          ex:Aircraft .

# Only ex:Sensor is profiled (two disjoint parts → no weak-supplementation noise).
ex:Sensor   logic:underMereologyProfile ex:MP .

# Two HolonicPositions for ex:Sensor — one per path, each a full five-place position
# (entity, holarchy, context, interval, path). The two differ by logic:positionPath, so
# logic:multiplyPositioned fires (the engine-verified path-relativity signal). The
# logic:holonicLevel literals and the min/max band are materialized OUTSIDE this all-IRI
# chase — see slices/core/logic/examples/holonic-band.ttl.
ex:posSensorDirect logic:positionEntity   ex:Sensor .
ex:posSensorDirect logic:positionHolarchy ex:H .
ex:posSensorDirect logic:positionContext  ex:OperationalContext .
ex:posSensorDirect logic:positionInterval ex:MissionInterval .
ex:posSensorDirect logic:positionPath     ex:pathDirect .

ex:posSensorVia    logic:positionEntity   ex:Sensor .
ex:posSensorVia    logic:positionHolarchy ex:H .
ex:posSensorVia    logic:positionContext  ex:OperationalContext .
ex:posSensorVia    logic:positionInterval ex:MissionInterval .
ex:posSensorVia    logic:positionPath     ex:pathVia .
